WEBVTT

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:19.120
So you're an all-out Yuuko-san supporter now?

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.080
Who are you supporting, Suzuko?

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:24.920
I'm in Sonati's camp.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:26.670
Huh? Sonata?

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:27.710
I'm placing my bets early.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:36.680
Hop. Hop.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:38.300
Hop!

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.640
Tsubasa's calling for us.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:43.480
Sonati, are you... a frog?

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.060
Bzzt!

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.190
I'm a bear!

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:48.020
I see.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:50.480
Beary-beary...

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:55.030
Ready, set, here we go!

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:58.070
AKB0048!

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:20.720
you won't be able to reach it yet.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.780
Even the stars of the sky

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:39.030
lie billions of lightyears away,

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:44.910
shining beyond the shadows.

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:51.170
Let me speak of hope,

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:57.260
like a nameless poet: with passion.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.470
you ni

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:57.260
atsuku

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:03.310
If you find yourself broken down in tears,

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:08.770
then rather than consoling you,

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:15.440
let me speak of the coming dawn.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:28.710
A few successors were recently invited to a peace ceremony on Kazakhstar.

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:26.990
- Kirara of Succession-

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:32.960
As this ceremony is in line with 00's philosophy,

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:35.170
we will most likely accept.

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:39.680
However, we cannot cancel the concert that it overlaps with.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:43.300
As a result, we've modified the stand-in system.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:44.890
Stand-in?

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:52.560
Um, that's when other members temporarily
replace the members who are in combat, right?

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:53.770
Correct.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:57.820
However, it had a slightly different meaning for the original AKB.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:00.570
When a member could not appear in concert,

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:03.870
another member or understudy would perform in their stead.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:06.080
They were known as "stand-ins".

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:08.290
Understudies, too?

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:12.330
Concerts on planets under the Entertainment Ban come with many dangers.

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:18.380
That's why only those who have completed their combat training are allowed on stage.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:22.640
However, with the tide turning in favor of entertainment,

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.510
that reasoning is no longer valid.

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:26.970
So we get to be stand-ins?

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:30.100
We can perform in place of successors?

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:33.940
Now, let me announce the stand-ins.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.280
Takamina's stand-in will be Shinonome Kanata.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:40.190
Understood!

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:42.660
Kojiharu's stand-in will be Kishida Mimori.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:43.700
Me?

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:44.530
Yay!

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.780
That's great, you two!

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:50.040
Next, Yukirin's stand-in: Wanibuchi Megumi.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:50.830
Okay!

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:53.790
All right!

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.920
And finally, Yuuko's stand-in:

00:03:58.590 --> 00:03:59.460
Sono Chieri.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:01.880
Right!

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:03.510
Whoa.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:06.890
Wow, you totally got your chance early!

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:08.060
That's wonderful, Chieri.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:10.430
Th-Thank you...

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:12.520
Why her?

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:17.150
The 76th generation should come before them in line for becoming stand-ins!

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:18.940
Why a 77th generation girl?

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:20.230
She's right.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:21.940
Isn't that weird?

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:26.700
Much like succession, seniority has no effect on your selection as a stand-in.

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:30.870
Unlike succession, however, the
essence of your soul is irrelevant.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.910
Selection is based on skill alone.

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:35.250
If you don't like it, practice more.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:37.040
That's the only way.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.510
Bringing back the stand-in
system for understudies, huh?

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:48.260
It's no surprise they'd object.

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:51.600
Yesterday, Sensei-sensei said...

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:56.150
<i>Stand-ins... Stand-ins...</i>

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:57.520
But Sensei...

00:04:58.310 --> 00:04:59.770
<i>Stand-ins...</i>

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:07.070
He has been much more proactively expressing his will lately.

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:08.780
Not to mention those lyrics...

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:10.870
The one about "enough something-or-other"?

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:12.660
Yes.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:17.080
Ever since the 77th generation appeared, it's as if he's been reacting to them.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:19.250
He keeps composing lyrics.

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:20.920
Which means...

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:29.890
So those of us who weren't chosen are on our own?

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:32.560
She said we could take the day off.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.230
How about it?

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:36.020
I'm telling you, it's not fair.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:40.440
Couldn't we at least get a corner of the room to practice in?

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.230
Hear hear!

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:43.070
You said it, Yuuka.

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:45.950
Fine then! We'll stuff ourselves and forget about them!

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:46.000
Tea

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:46.990
Sounds like a plan!

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:51.080
It's the 76th generation girls.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:55.330
On second thought...

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:57.460
This stinks!

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:00.380
Ugh, I <i>hate</i> these sorts of awkward situations.

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:01.210
Fine!

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:03.420
Since we have the day off, let's go have fun!

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:05.420
Let's go to karaoke! Let's go all out!

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:06.170
Yeah!

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:07.470
Sonata wants to karaoke!

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.390
Are you coming too, Nagisa?

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.470
No thanks.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:13.350
I'll just relax in the dorm.

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:19.480
Nagisa-san is a Yuuko-san supporter, after all.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:20.610
Yeah...

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:30.780
<i>This is nothing...</i>

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:32.700
Onwards! Onwards!

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:34.990
Straight on ahead!

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:35.330
<i>like our usual lessons.</i>

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:36.580
Cross that river!

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:39.120
Ho! Ho! Ho! Ho!

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:40.330
<i>It's a whole new level!</i>

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:38.830
Ho!

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:43.290
Our dreams always

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:45.630
seem so far off.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:49.800
It feels like I'll never make it.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.550
No, that's not how it goes!

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:57.310
<i>Before your eyes,</i>

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:00.100
<i>there flows a river:</i>

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:00.600
<i>A wide—</i>

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:01.650
Stop!

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:07.280
You gotta show more emotion!

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:09.740
Otherwise, the crowd won't feel you.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:21.000
<i>Hang on to your dreams until the day they come true.</i>

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.920
<i>Cross that river! You can do it!</i>

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.010
Perfect!

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:30.090
Really?

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:33.260
Yep. I'm glad you're my stand-in.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:38.890
The original Takamina-san had more
passion and leadership than anyone else.

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:42.020
Just like how you're captain of the understudies.

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:43.230
Takamina-san!

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:47.270
Also, slow down when you're
supposed to, or you'll lose the rhythm.

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:47.980
Got it!

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.990
Okay! That's it for this morning.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:51.950
Be ready for another workout tonight!

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:52.740
Okay!

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:55.030
Man, I'm starving!

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:56.660
Wonder what's for lunch today.

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:57.910
Green pepper steak, I think.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:07:59.830
Ugh, peppers?

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:00.160
Chieri!

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:01.330
Yes?

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.420
We're done here. Time for lunch.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:03.830
But...

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:08.920
If you don't eat well, you won't last the whole set list.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:12.430
You gotta shovel down that food and build those muscles!

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:15.140
Okay...

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:18.890
Too many freakin' peppers!

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:21.180
I'm done.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:21.730
Righto!

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:28.480
<i>I guess I'm just not up to par yet.</i>

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:29.900
I'm starving!

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:31.610
Welcome back!

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:33.200
How were the lessons?

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.660
Way harder than I imagined.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:36.620
Sounds intense.

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:41.700
So intense that my hips are still trembling!

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:43.710
Are you okay, Mimori-san?

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:48.920
Chieri-chan, you don't like peppers, do you?

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:50.130
That's right.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:52.380
I went easy on the peppers.

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:53.470
Thank you.

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:55.220
That was great.

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:58.180
Chef Papa! The peppers were delicious!

00:08:58.180 --> 00:08:59.470
Thanks!

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:03.020
Actually, give me extra peppers!

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:05.020
Oh? Up for the challenge, are you?

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:07.060
Then I'll load 'er up!

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:08.900
Oh no, I'm even sweating down <i>here...</i>

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:10.190
Chieri...

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:31.420
Sexy!

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:36.130
All right! Feeling on top of the world!

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:41.100
<i>I want you! I need you!</i>

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:42.850
<i>I love you!</i>

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:43.640
Okay!

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:46.640
S-Sexy...

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:52.320
Chieri, what in the world are you doing?

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:55.280
N-No, I'm just...

00:09:58.570 --> 00:09:59.740
Sorry.

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:03.790
You're doing your best to be like Yuuko-san, aren't you?

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:05.120
Yeah.

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:07.040
I'm kind of glad.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.000
Huh?

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.130
By the way...

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:12.630
congrats on becoming a stand-in.

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:14.710
I realized I hadn't said it yet.

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:18.260
Thanks.

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:26.680
Hey, before you go to evening lessons, want to take a look at my Yuuko-san notebook?

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:28.600
Yuuko-san notebook?

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:31.610
Yep. An all-about-Yuuko-san notebook!

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:32.980
Chieri.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:37.490
Isn't there something you've been hiding from us?

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:38.360
Huh?

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:40.360
Don't pretend you don't know.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:42.240
Guess what we found?

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.410
The Case of the CEO's Daughter

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.410
Sudden disappearance...

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.410
the cause?

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:47.710
Your dad runs Zodiac Corporation, doesn't he?

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:50.040
Relationship with DES

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:50.040
Tension between

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:50.040
father and daughter

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:52.080
That machine...

00:10:56.630 --> 00:11:00.800
So your daddy's company makes DES's weapons, huh?

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:02.640
I smell a rat. A stinky, stinky rat.

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:04.680
Chieri, are you a DES spy or what?

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:06.100
How could you? A spy?

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:07.980
But it's way suspicious!

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:09.480
Kanata.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:10.940
What is it? What's going on here?

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:12.270
Take a look at this article.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:15.480
Chieri...

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:19.240
Wait!

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:22.160
Relationship with DES

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:22.160
Tension between

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:22.160
father and daughter

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:38.260
You know... ever since that
concert, I've wanted to join 00.

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:41.970
But even though I kept asking my father to let me audition,

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:43.970
he simply refused to budge.

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:55.940
I refused to give up, so I secretly attended another 00 concert.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:59.690
That day, DES attacked,

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:04.620
and I saw that their machines were from my father's company.

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:09.910
So when I heard about the
audition, I ran away from home.

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:14.630
Of course, the others must see me

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:17.750
as the untrustworthy daughter of their sworn enemy.

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:21.840
I knew that I didn't belong here.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.300
That's not true!

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:26.430
I want to become a successor with you and stand by your side on stage!

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:30.720
Sorry... but could you give me some time alone?

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:37.820
Karaoke

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:48.450
Though I'm surrounded by all these other girls,

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:47.450
In the end...

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:49.120
A Midsummer Sounds Good

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:49.120
Stand Up, Girls

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:49.120
It's all AKB songs.

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:51.950
everyone's eyes will be fixed on me.

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:53.120
It's fun to have singing practice like this sometimes.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:55.170
I get it.

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:55.460
This is <i>not</i> practice! It's karaoke!

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:58.170
We won't become stand-ins at this rate.

00:12:55.460 --> 00:13:02.130
The stage is a chaotic mess,

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:03.170
Actually practicing is our best bet.

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:04.260
but we're all gonna rise up,

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:06.430
leave our competition in the dust,

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:09.050
and make our way to the elections!

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:11.140
<i>Aim to be a stand-in!</i>

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:14.600
<i>We'll make it to Position 0 like a tiger!</i>

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:14.600
Don't interrupt!

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:17.190
Okay, good work!

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:21.900
Successors are dismissed.
Stand-ins, please remain.

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:23.490
Thank you very much!

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:25.650
Chieri never came back.

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:28.120
Yeah... wonder what happened.

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:29.620
Ushiyama-sensei!

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:32.830
Excuse me. I'm going to go get Chieri!

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:34.750
Stop!

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:39.920
I understand you're worried
about your fellow understudy.

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:43.300
However, you now have a duty as a stand-in.

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:45.630
Duty...

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:48.090
Chieri abandoned her duty.

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:51.140
You can't waste time on someone like her.

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:54.640
You're close to being promoted, you know.

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:58.350
Even so, please let me go.

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:01.610
My duty as captain of the understudies comes before my duty as a stand-in.

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:03.820
I can't just leave her be!

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:06.150
Kanata.

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:08.820
She's a fierce one.

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:12.410
Okay! You two had better practice hard.

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:13.910
Right!

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:21.540
You know, practicing together really drove the point home,

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:26.170
but I think Kanata's skills are at successor level already.

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:29.220
I see where you're coming from.

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:34.640
Thing is, none of us know how succession is decided.

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:38.390
I was thinking of discussing it with Tsubasa-san.

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:40.940
We'll ask her to make Kanata a successor!

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.320
That's our captain!

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:46.070
Takamina forever! I love you!

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:46.610
Smooch!

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:50.530
While you're at it, I think I'll join.

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:51.990
As will I.

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:53.080
Great! Come on!

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:53.700
Wait!

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:54.830
Stop!

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:56.660
Smooch~

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:10.220
We're forbidden from entering that place.

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:11.760
What's your call, Takamina?

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:13.050
Should we give up?

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:18.270
Wai—

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:20.350
Mayuyu!

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:28.280
Well, we're in...

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:30.950
but completely lost.

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:36.660
Still, I had no idea there was such a huge space under the concert hall.

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:38.000
That's for sure.

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:52.590
Wow!

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:54.760
Are these all Kirara?

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:06.520
Is that... the original Ooshima Yuuko?

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.230
She is!

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:10.440
What could be happening here?

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:14.200
It's the original Yukirin!

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.700
She's so cute!

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:18.870
But why are the originals...

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:21.460
Mirrors of the soul.

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:28.460
That's it! These Kirara must reflect the face
of the original member you're succeeding.

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:30.710
Wow, that's nifty.

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:42.140
Huh? That face...

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:54.450
The original Takamina?

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:01.500
Kanata?

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:02.870
What's going on?

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:19.140
What are you trying to do?

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:21.850
I'm sorry for not telling you before.

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:24.100
You didn't answer my question.

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:29.520
I took the auditions without
mentioning what my father does.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:32.400
I have no right to be here.

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:34.240
This isn't about your father!

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:39.830
My father was killed by DES.

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:45.910
I joined 00 to avenge him.

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:49.750
Remember what you said, Chieri.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:52.090
<i>There's still a lot I don't understand.</i>

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:55.720
I'm counting on the more experienced girls to set a good example.

00:17:56.630 --> 00:18:00.350
That knocked some sense into me.

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:04.220
I used to be all gung-ho about getting revenge,

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:06.600
but now it's more than that.

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:10.730
I want to become a successor.

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:13.570
Kanata-san.

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:19.160
Your father shouldn't affect your decision either.

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:21.370
Your dream is what matters.

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:26.330
Isn't that why you never mentioned it?

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:37.470
I didn't expect that.

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:41.430
You're just like a child when you cry.

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:46.140
Come on, I've already got Sonata to take care of.

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:52.770
Don't bottle everything up inside until you have no way out.

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:56.190
Of course, I'm hardly one to talk.

00:18:56.190 --> 00:19:00.780
But we can move past that together.

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:07.120
We have friends now, who will share our joy and sadness.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:10.040
Friends...

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:14.250
Chieri, I was—

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:19.340
U-Um, I'msorryforbarginginon...

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:21.550
Silly. It's not what you think.

00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:23.970
You see?

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:38.320
What are you doing?!

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:40.990
This is sacred ground! You shouldn't be here!

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:42.280
What's this supposed to mean?

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:49.710
The original Takamina... turned into Kanata...

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:51.710
Why wasn't it me?

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:57.050
The Kirara here are Kirara of Succession.

00:19:57.750 --> 00:19:59.760
Kirara of Succession...

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:07.260
Try as we might, we must still rely on external forces to choose successors.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:11.480
These Kirara, on the other hand,
can sense the essence of one's soul.

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:13.230
Then...

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:21.110
Up until a year ago, the Kirara chose you as Takamina—as Takahashi Minami.

00:20:22.110 --> 00:20:25.030
However, as Kanata's power increased,

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:31.660
they began to show her instead.

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:35.920
Her soul is the one closest to
the original Takahashi Minami.

00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:40.670
Her soul... is the closest...?

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:47.350
The Kirara of Succession choose Kanata as Takahashi Minami.

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:50.970
When you graduate, the next Takahashi Minami will be her.

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:57.110
Then she won't be promoted unless I graduate?

00:20:57.110 --> 00:20:58.400
Yes.

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:04.450
However, the Kirara of Succession
here do no more than reflect souls.

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:07.280
None of us are hoping that you'll graduate.

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:12.120
But you always say that succession depends not only on appearance or personality,

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:15.790
but on the essence of your soul...

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:20.840
The essence of your soul is not the only factor.

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:24.010
Experience, cooperativeness, and timing also matter.

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:27.640
Kanata may have grown closer to Takahashi Minami,

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:29.970
but you were chosen once, too.

00:21:29.970 --> 00:21:32.270
As captain, you must keep your chin up.

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:35.100
That's what's best for 0048.

00:21:36.730 --> 00:21:37.350
Takamina.

00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:39.110
Takamina!

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:45.490
You girls, make sure—

00:21:45.490 --> 00:21:48.320
Of course we won't tell anyone!

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:49.120
Because...

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:53.580
She's our Takamina. She's the captain of 00.

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:55.290
No one can take her place!

00:22:21.310 --> 00:22:23.690
The stars that shine in the night sky

00:22:21.310 --> 00:22:23.690
yoru no sora kagayaku hoshi wa

00:22:23.690 --> 00:22:26.280
lie billions of lightyears away.

00:22:23.690 --> 00:22:26.280
nanoku kounen no kanata

00:22:26.280 --> 00:22:28.820
Even if the depths of despair

00:22:26.280 --> 00:22:27.070
tatoe fukai zetsubou ga

00:22:27.070 --> 00:22:28.820
tatoe fukai zetsubou ga

